{"role":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. The main one about **radon as a gas** is **2024 LQ Q13**.\n\n### 2024 Paper 1B Q13 (radon gas)\nRn-222: colourless, odourless radioactive gas from bedrock/granite concrete; half-life 3.82 days; α-emitter.\n\n**(a)(i)** Decay constant  \nλ = ln 2 / T½ ≈ **2.1 × 10⁻⁶ s⁻¹**\n\n**(a)(ii)** With A ≈ 48 Bq m⁻³:  \nN = A / λ ≈ **2.3 × 10⁷** atoms per m³\n\n**(a)(iii)** Harmful because radon is a **gas that can be inhaled**; α particles then ionize lung tissue from inside (even though α has low penetrating power outside the body).\n\n---\n\n### Also mentions radon (decay product, not “radon gas” hazards)\n| Paper | Topic |\n|---|---|\n| **2014 MC Q33** | Ra → Rn + α; mass defect from 4.9 MeV. **Answer: C** (products ~8.7 × 10⁻³⁰ kg **less**) |\n| **2018 LQ Q10** | Ra-226 decay series to radon |\n| **2012 LQ Q11** | Ra-226 α-decay to radon; nuclear equation + energy |\n\nSo for **indoor radon / harm of radon gas**, use **2024 Q13**."}]}}
